1017
00:53:21,140 --> 00:53:22,652
So when is actually helpful?

1018
00:53:22,652 --> 00:53:23,860
I actually would debate that.

1019
00:53:23,860 --> 00:53:25,527
So I think even--
it's a great question.

1020
00:53:25,527 --> 00:53:26,945
I think maybe it
partly depends on

1021
00:53:26,945 --> 00:53:28,570
how you're thinking
of the state space.

1022
00:53:28,570 --> 00:53:31,990
But I think if your state, say,
for-- let's say I'm driving.

1023
00:53:31,990 --> 00:53:35,335
If my state is just
my immediate position,

1024
00:53:35,335 --> 00:53:36,460
that's probably not enough.

1025
00:53:36,460 --> 00:53:37,960
I probably need at
least my last few

1026
00:53:37,960 --> 00:53:39,687
to get to velocity
and acceleration.

1027
00:53:39,687 --> 00:53:41,770
So you might already be
thinking, oh, in my state,

1028
00:53:41,770 --> 00:53:42,770
they already have those.

1029
00:53:42,770 --> 00:53:44,610
If that's the case,
if your state already

1030
00:53:44,610 --> 00:53:47,340
incorporates like something
about the first or second order

1031
00:53:47,340 --> 00:53:50,350
derivatives, that's
